Q: Node fs copy a folder A: <p>Node 16.7.0 added experimental support for <a href="https://nodejs.org/api/fs.html#fscpsrc-dest-options-callback" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>fs.cp</code></a> and <a href="https://nodejs.org/api/fs.html#fscpsyncsrc-dest-options" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>fs.cpSync</code></a>:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>(A)synchronously copies the entire directory structure from src to dest, including subdirectories and files.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The APIs became stable in Node.js 22.3.0.</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>// asynchronous
fs.cp(src, dest, { recursive: true }, (err) =&gt; {/* callback */});

// synchronous
fs.cpSync(src, dest, { recursive: true });
</code></pre>

Q: How to align divs with ul and li to be centered to the | separator? A: <p>Use <code>display:grid</code> with two columns, then text align as required.</p>
<p><a href="https://i.sstatic.net/wiRAaLZY.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/wiRAaLZY.png" alt="enter image description here" /></a></p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>* {
  margin: 0;
